f.block("      const EN_NOTE = 'The neighborhood in the Scout Engine:", "\n", "      const EN_NOTE = 'The neighborhood in the Scout Engine: every building the dashboard holds on its FEMA footprint at its recorded height (a usual one for its kind where none is on file) under a physical sky, the city going on to the skyline. Roof View reads every roof eight ways: what covers it, which shingle it is, how hot it runs, how worn it is, what the weather on the scales would do to it, its fire class and zone, the sun it takes and the cool roof rule, and the damage most likely over the next 15 years. The rain scale runs from light rain to a rank 5 atmospheric river, the dry wind scale to an extreme offshore wind day. Walk, circle a building or fly an Alta X; past light rain the Alta X stays on the ground, and the flying saucer and the Tic Tac fly instead and warp to any address or coordinates in California. Window grids, cars, signals, sidewalks, rooftop equipment, the weather and the craft are generated, not observed; the roof views are a model, not an inspection.';")
